window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-084.json",{"day":84,"title":"Finding Time to Pay Attention","targetWords":[{"word":"time","gloss":"时间","context":"Once these discoveries were discussed, the routine felt less like lost time and more like an opportunity to understand where they lived.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"when","gloss":"什么时候","context":"She then asked when they had last noticed something surprising on the way to school.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"year","gloss":"年","context":"At the end of a recent year, a teacher asked her students to describe a day they could still remember clearly.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"two","gloss":"二","context":"At first, two students said the exercise was pointless; three admitted they often checked messages without any particular reason.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"four","gloss":"四","context":"After four days, however, their notes became more detailed.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"now","gloss":"现在","context":"During a discussion of an event that occurred early in the term, the class discovered how differently they understood it now and then.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"then","gloss":"当时","context":"She then asked when they had last noticed something surprising on the way to school.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"minute","gloss":"分钟","context":"They had become accustomed to treating each minute as a unit to fill, while attention moved toward the next task before the present one had properly begun.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"after","gloss":"在…之后","context":"After four days, however, their notes became more detailed.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"three","gloss":"三","context":"At first, two students said the exercise was pointless; three admitted they often checked messages without any particular reason.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"end","gloss":"结束","context":"At the end of a recent year, a teacher asked her students to describe a day they could still remember clearly.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"once","gloss":"一旦","context":"Once these discoveries were discussed, the routine felt less like lost time and more like an opportunity to understand where they lived.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"day","gloss":"日子","context":"At the end of a recent year, a teacher asked her students to describe a day they could still remember clearly.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"before","gloss":"在…之前","context":"They had become accustomed to treating each minute as a unit to fill, while attention moved toward the next task before the present one had properly begun.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"often","gloss":"经常","context":"At first, two students said the exercise was pointless; three admitted they often checked messages without any particular reason.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"old","gloss":"老的","context":"An old shop sign prompted a question about local history, and a conversation with a neighbor revealed changes made ten years ago.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"while","gloss":"当…时","context":"They had become accustomed to treating each minute as a unit to fill, while attention moved toward the next task before the present one had properly begun.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"last","gloss":"上一次","context":"She then asked when they had last noticed something surprising on the way to school.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"still","gloss":"仍然","context":"At the end of a recent year, a teacher asked her students to describe a day they could still remember clearly.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"second","gloss":"第二次","context":"Today, news arrives so quickly that yesterday's concern appears late by the second update.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"during","gloss":"在…期间","context":"During a discussion of an event that occurred early in the term, the class discovered how differently they understood it now and then.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"age","gloss":"年龄","context":"The teacher connected these observations to the experience of age.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hour","gloss":"小时","context":"A child may feel that an hour lasts forever, yet an adult can struggle to remember an entire month.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"early","gloss":"早期的","context":"During a discussion of an event that occurred early in the term, the class discovered how differently they understood it now and then.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"today","gloss":"在今天","context":"Today, news arrives so quickly that yesterday's concern appears late by the second update.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"since","gloss":"因为","context":"Since familiar routines require fewer new decisions, they can leave fewer distinctive memories.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"future","gloss":"未来","context":"This does not mean that the past was always richer or that the future must be empty.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"yet","gloss":"然而","context":"A child may feel that an hour lasts forever, yet an adult can struggle to remember an entire month.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"never","gloss":"从不","context":"The teacher never asked them to record everything; a life devoted to perfect documentation would leave little room for living.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"century","gloss":"世纪","context":"A century can seem remote until a family photograph gives it a human face.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"always","gloss":"总是","context":"This does not mean that the past was always richer or that the future must be empty.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"week","gloss":"周","context":"For one week, they would spend five minutes observing their surroundings before using a phone.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ten","gloss":"十","context":"An old shop sign prompted a question about local history, and a conversation with a neighbor revealed changes made ten years ago.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"past","gloss":"过去","context":"This does not mean that the past was always richer or that the future must be empty.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"present","gloss":"现在","context":"They had become accustomed to treating each minute as a unit to fill, while attention moved toward the next task before the present one had properly begun.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"five","gloss":"五","context":"For one week, they would spend five minutes observing their surroundings before using a phone.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"recent","gloss":"近来的","context":"At the end of a recent year, a teacher asked her students to describe a day they could still remember clearly.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"next","gloss":"下一个","context":"They had become accustomed to treating each minute as a unit to fill, while attention moved toward the next task before the present one had properly begun.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"history","gloss":"历史","context":"An old shop sign prompted a question about local history, and a conversation with a neighbor revealed changes made ten years ago.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"almost","gloss":"几乎","context":"Almost everyone chose an unusual event rather than an ordinary lesson.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"ago","gloss":"以前","context":"An old shop sign prompted a question about local history, and a conversation with a neighbor revealed changes made ten years ago.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ever","gloss":"曾经","context":"Someone who says nothing interesting has ever happened may already have overlooked events worth recalling, rather than actually having lived without them.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"late","gloss":"晚的","context":"Today, news arrives so quickly that yesterday's concern appears late by the second update.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"until","gloss":"直到","context":"A century can seem remote until a family photograph gives it a human face.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"already","gloss":"已经","context":"Someone who says nothing interesting has ever happened may already have overlooked events worth recalling, rather than actually having lived without them.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"month","gloss":"月","context":"A child may feel that an hour lasts forever, yet an adult can struggle to remember an entire month.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"opportunity","gloss":"机会","context":"Once these discoveries were discussed, the routine felt less like lost time and more like an opportunity to understand where they lived.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"decade","gloss":"十年","context":"A decade becomes meaningful through changes in work, housing, and relationships.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"third","gloss":"第三次","context":"By the third meeting, nobody claimed the exercise had solved every distraction.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"again","gloss":"再次","context":"What had changed was their willingness to begin again.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"At the end of a recent year, a teacher asked her students to describe a day they could still remember clearly. Almost everyone chose an unusual event rather than an ordinary lesson. She then asked when they had last noticed something surprising on the way to school. Many could not answer. The problem was not that their lives contained no interesting details. They had become accustomed to treating each minute as a unit to fill, while attention moved toward the next task before the present one had properly begun.","zh":"最近一年结束时，一位教师请学生描述至今仍记得清楚的一天。几乎每个人都选择了不寻常事件，而不是普通课堂。她又问，大家上次在上学路上注意到惊喜是什么时候。很多人无法回答。问题不是生活缺乏有趣细节，而是大家习惯把每分钟当作需要填满的单位，当前任务尚未真正开始，注意力就转向下一项。"},{"en":"The class experimented with a small change. For one week, they would spend five minutes observing their surroundings before using a phone. At first, two students said the exercise was pointless; three admitted they often checked messages without any particular reason. After four days, however, their notes became more detailed. An old shop sign prompted a question about local history, and a conversation with a neighbor revealed changes made ten years ago. Once these discoveries were discussed, the routine felt less like lost time and more like an opportunity to understand where they lived.","zh":"全班尝试了一个小改变。一周内，他们在用手机前先花五分钟观察周围。起初，两名学生说练习没有意义，三名承认自己常无缘无故查看消息。但四天之后，笔记变得更细致。旧商店招牌引发地方历史的问题，与邻居交谈揭示了十年前的变化。发现得到讨论之后，练习不再像浪费时间，而更像了解居住环境的机会。"},{"en":"The teacher connected these observations to the experience of age. A child may feel that an hour lasts forever, yet an adult can struggle to remember an entire month. Since familiar routines require fewer new decisions, they can leave fewer distinctive memories. This does not mean that the past was always richer or that the future must be empty. It suggests that attention helps shape what remains available to memory. Someone who says nothing interesting has ever happened may already have overlooked events worth recalling, rather than actually having lived without them.","zh":"教师把观察与年龄体验联系起来。孩子可能觉得一小时长得没完，成年人却可能很难回忆整个月。熟悉惯例需要较少的新决定，因此可能留下较少独特记忆。这并不意味着过去总更丰富，也不意味着未来必然空洞，而是说明注意力有助于决定哪些内容留给记忆。说自己从未遇到有趣事情的人，可能已经忽略了值得回想的事件，而不是真的没有经历过。"},{"en":"Students also considered longer scales. A century can seem remote until a family photograph gives it a human face. A decade becomes meaningful through changes in work, housing, and relationships. Today, news arrives so quickly that yesterday's concern appears late by the second update. Yet speed alone does not explain importance. During a discussion of an event that occurred early in the term, the class discovered how differently they understood it now and then. They learned to resist the assumption that a newer account automatically deserves greater trust than an older one.","zh":"学生也考虑更长的时间尺度。一个世纪似乎遥远，直到家庭照片赋予它人的面孔。十年通过工作、住房和关系变化获得意义。如今，新闻来得如此快，昨天关注的事情在第二次更新时似乎已经过时。但速度本身不能说明重要性。讨论学期初发生的事情时，全班发现现在与当时的理解很不一样。他们学会反对一种假设：较新的叙述必然比较旧的叙述更值得信任。"},{"en":"By the third meeting, nobody claimed the exercise had solved every distraction. They still missed details and sometimes rushed until exhaustion. What had changed was their willingness to begin again. The teacher never asked them to record everything; a life devoted to perfect documentation would leave little room for living. Instead, she suggested a modest practice: pause occasionally, notice what has changed, and ask why it matters. Attention could not make time stop, but it could prevent every passing experience from becoming indistinguishable from the one before it.","zh":"第三次聚会时，没有人声称练习解决了所有分心。大家仍漏掉细节，有时一直匆忙到筋疲力尽。改变的是愿意再次开始。教师从未要求记录一切，完全致力于完美记录的生活会不给真正生活留下多少空间。她建议一种适度实践：偶尔停顿，注意哪些东西改变，询问它为何重要。注意力无法让时间停下，却可以避免每段逝去经历都与上一段毫无区别。"}],"previous":83,"next":85});
